      "number": 1,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "Which of the following conclusion is correct if the ratio test is applied to the series\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{3^n \\cdot n^3}{n!} \\quad ?\n$$",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "The series is conditionally convergent because $r = 1$."
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "The series is absolutely convergent because $r = 1/3$."
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "The series is divergent because $r = 3$."
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "The series is absolutely convergent because $r = 0$."
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "The ratio test is inconclusive because $r = 1$."
        }
      ],
      "answer": "D",
