      "number": 3,
      "points": 9,
      "stem": "Given two arbitrary series $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n$ and $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} b_n$, determine which of the following three statements is/are always TRUE.\n\n(i) If $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n$ and $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} b_n$ are both convergent, then $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n - b_n$ is convergent.\n\n(ii) If $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n$ and $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} b_n$ are both divergent, then $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n + b_n$ is divergent.\n\n(iii) If $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n$ and $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} b_n$ are both divergent, then $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} a_n b_n$ is divergent.\n\nNote: Partial credit is possible for this question.",
      "choices": [
